      'Every cell in the body needs a steady supply of fuel and building materials, but the food we eat arrives as large, complex pieces: meat, bread, vegetables. The cells cannot use these directly. The job of the digestive system is to take food in, break it down into molecules small enough to cross into the blood, absorb them, and get rid of whatever is left.',
