      'The pancreas is really two organs in one. Most of it is exocrine tissue, which makes pancreatic juice and sends it through ducts into the duodenum. Scattered within it are small clusters of endocrine cells, the islets of Langerhans, which make insulin and glucagon and release them into the blood.',
